 "text": "9/29/26, 10:16 AM\n\nAutomatic Release\n\nUse\n\nYou want to release receivables for collection in other business transactions.\n\nIntegration\n\nThe release of receivables for collection is integrated in the following business processes:\n\ne Dunning\ne Write-off\n\ne Write-off in mass run\n\nKey Features\n\nIf you make the relevant system settings, items that have reached a certain dunning level are automatically released for collection.\n\nIf you select the Release Receivables for Submission to Collection Agency indicator during manual write-off or in the write-off\n\nrun, the receivables written off are automatically released for collection.\n\nDuring the release, the programs determine the items to be released, release the positions, and set the submission status 01\n(Receivable Released for Submission). The document is given the collection item number OO1. The collection agency is\ndetermined in event 5060.\n\nActivities\nDunning\n\nIf you want to release items automatically in the dunning run, in Customizing for Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable, under\nBusiness Transactions \u00bb Dunning Notices\u00bb Configure Dunning Activities \u201c, define a relevant dunning activity and enter the\n\nfunction module FKK_COLL_AGENCY_RELEASE_0350 for this activity. The function module is processed in the dunning run. If the\ndunning level is reached, the module selects the items and releases them automatically. See also the documentation for the\nCustomizing activity.\n\nWrite-Off\n\n1. In the SAP Easy Access menu, choose |sAccount . Write Off Items \u201cJ (transaction FP04).\n\n2. Then proceed as described in the section Writing Off Items.\nMass Write-Off\n\n1. In the SAP Easy Access screen, choose |}*Periodic Processing \u00bb For Contract Accounts \u00bb Write-Off Run 3 (transaction\nFPO4M).\n\n2. Then proceed as described in the section Writing Off Items in Mass Runs.\n",
